    {
      "id": "OC-4",
      "severity": "verify-only-if-XPC-is-ever-selected",
      "statement": "If a sandboxed XPC Mach service is EVER selected as the macOS host-to-provider channel, the endpoint name must be prefixed by an App Group ID the sandboxed process is entitled to. TASK-260728-7ii1xz evaluated that channel as candidate C and rejected it, and rule G4 now prohibits com.apple.security.application-groups on every macOS target, so no macOS target holds a group prefix today and the question is dormant rather than pending. Every Apple example of the pattern found, and all three shipping products inspected on this Mac, use a macOS-style Team-ID-prefixed group for the prefix - and all of those predate the Feb 2025 change.",
      "affects": [
        "TASK-260715-uyju7n",
        "TASK-260715-3f4lxy"
      ],
      "resolutionOwner": "TASK-260715-ypo7yo",
      "matrixEffect": "none - dormant. macOS App Groups are prohibited under rule G4, so no macOS target carries a group prefix. If XPC is ever revived, that is a G4 reopening case (a) and this matrix is amended under section 11; only then does the iOS-style-prefix question need settling, and if an iOS-style prefix were rejected the amendment would add a SEPARATE, unregistrable macOS-style identifier for that single purpose, leaving the registered iOS-style records untouched.",
      "newEvidenceR4": "Read at /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb on macOS 26.5 (25F71): application.sb:326-328 builds the authorized prefix as (global-name-prefix (string-append suite \".\")) where suite is the literal entitlement value, whatever its style. On the SANDBOX side the mechanism is therefore style-agnostic, and an iOS-style group.works.relux.tunnel would yield the prefix 'group.works.relux.tunnel.'. This is evidence, not proof: the launchd bootstrap-registration side and the profile-authorization side were not exercised, and nothing was signed. Recorded so a future revival of the XPC channel starts from what is known rather than from the r3 statement that no source addressed it at all.",
      "notAStopTheLine": "The question is only reachable if a rejected candidate is revived, it has a named owner, and it does not block Ceremony C1 - C1 no longer grants the App Groups capability at all."
    }
